From: JavaScript_X <73346071+JavaScript-X@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: treat the BCM6362 integrated WLAN as 2.4 GHz only

The radio of the BCM6362 SoC WLAN (d11 corerev 22, radio 2057 rev 8) has no
5 GHz support in b43 (no 5 GHz IPA gain table) and SFR Neufbox 6 boards have
no 5 GHz front-end. Advertising band 2 only makes channel switches fail.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -5388,6 +5388,10 @@
 
 	/* Note: below IDs can be "virtual" (not maching e.g. real PCI ID) */
 	switch (dev_id) {
+	case 0x435f: /* BCM6362 integrated WLAN: radio 2057 rev 8, 2.4 GHz only */
+		*have_2ghz_phy = true;
+		*have_5ghz_phy = false;
+		return;
 	case 0x4324: /* BCM4306 */
 	case 0x4312: /* BCM4311 */
 	case 0x4319: /* BCM4318 */
@@ -5396,7 +5400,6 @@
 	case 0x4350: /* BCM43222 */
 	case 0x4353: /* BCM43224 */
 	case 0x0576: /* BCM43224 */
-	case 0x435f: /* BCM6362 */
 	case 0x4331: /* BCM4331 */
 	case 0x4359: /* BCM43228 */
 	case 0x43a0: /* BCM4360 */
